<title>UK: BA chief joins Major on India trade mission.</title>
<headline>BA chief joins Major on India trade mission.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc said on Wednesday its Chief Executive Robert Ayling joined British Prime Minister John Major on a trade mission to India to try to promote further access for air services between the countries.</p>
<p>BA said it was allowed to operate 16 weekly flights from Britain to India but would like to raise that number to cope with rising demand.</p>
<p>The airline said officials from both governments will resume talks in late spring on improving access.</p>
<p>Major is scheduled to visit India, Pakistan and Bangladesh.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
